  "description": "Full PACE-CAM AES-128 session, ICAO 9303 Part 11 App I.1 (Brainpool P-256). CAM runs the GM flow on the wire (§4.4.3.3.3: the mapping phase is identical to Generic Mapping), and the final GA response carries the real App I.1 DO8A after the DO86 token. The port consumes it: the step-4 tag-scan extracts the DO8A, decrypts it with IV = E(KSenc, -1) and exposes CA_IC on PACEHandler.camData (beyond upstream, whose extraction is commented out, so it ignores the record). Consuming it changes nothing on the wire, which is why this fixture stays both-runner: the Swift replay drives the same bytes to the same session keys and simply does not read the DO8A. GA rounds are byte-for-byte the App I.1 listings; the MSE:Set AT carries DO84 (parameterId 13), which the App I listing omits. Post-PACE SELECT under the installed AES SM (keys 0A9D.../4B1C... from App I.1). That the Dart replay recovers App I.1's published CA_IC 85DC3FA9...53C426B3 from these exact bytes is asserted in test/conformance/pace_can_cam_transcripts_test.dart: the transcript schema has no field for it. runners omitted = both.",
